cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AMT.engine: Academic Meta Tool reasoning engine"
abstract: >-
  AMT.engine is a pure-Python reasoner for the Academic Meta Tool ontology.
  It reads a Turtle file with concepts, roles and weighted assertions, applies
  n-ary role-chain inference with six fuzzy-logic operators and role
  subsumption, validates the input with SHACL and exports the result as
  RDF/Turtle, Neo4J Cypher, CSV and an interactive HTML graph.
type: software
